       ssiiggnnbbiitt()  is a generic macro which can work on all real floating‐point
       types.  It returns a nonzero value if the value of _x has its  sign  bit
       set.

       This is not the same as _x _< _0_._0, because IEEE 754 floating point allows
       zero  to  be  signed.   The  comparison  _-_0_._0 _< _0_._0 is false, but _s_i_g_n_‐
       _b_i_t_(_-_0_._0_) will return a nonzero value.

       NaNs and infinities have a sign bit.

